# Sub-tick interpolation of the moby ground shadows
# (tests/harness/check_shadow_subtick.sh).
#   <bk2> | <V> | blob=<x>,<y> ... [tol=<px>] [step=<px>] [judge=<a>,...]
# V is the canonical VBL the intermediate present at V+1 sits above; V-2 opens
# the interval that present covers. V is even because a tick spans two VBLs
# here: the intermediate present at V+1 has to fall inside V's own tick.
#
# Sheila kicks a rock across the ledge over these two ticks. Each row names two
# shadows: the rock's, which moves through the world, and a second shadow near
# (397,315) whose moby stands still, so its whole canonical step is the
# camera's. The second is the control — a shadow the moby's own translation
# cannot reach, which stayed inside 0.25 px of the lerp while the rock's stood
# a whole tick step away — and it is also the reason the engagement leg asks
# only that one of a row's blobs hold its tick pose under
# OPENPETE_SHADOW_INTERP=0: the static one cannot.
#
# The bound is 1.0 px, twice the glint harness's, because the decal's size is a
# channel this fix does not carry: the drawn-moby list's per-entry radius word
# and its membership are the newest tick's, so the mask's area ramps across the
# interval and the visible centroid follows it wherever the decal is clipped by
# terrain.
sheilas-alp-sheila-water-invisible.bk2 | 4532 | blob=490.2,271.4 blob=397.4,314.5 tol=1.0
sheilas-alp-sheila-water-invisible.bk2 | 4534 | blob=469.2,274.0 blob=391.5,320.8 tol=1.0
